As a chronic Tolkein fan, I have recently wondered why Orcrist is a 
two-handed sword.
It is apparent from Gandalf's fight with the Balrog on the Bridge of
Khazad Dum that Glamdring is not a two-handed sword, since the wizard
held his staff in his left hand, but in his right "Glamdring gleamed,
cold and white" (or something like that).
I assume Orcrist and Glamdring are of the same design (since they are
"mates", (Beater and Biter)). Hence Orcrist should not be a two-handed
sword (perhaps it should be yet another long sword).
Any other Tolkein addicts out there care to comment, or supply further
information?

